Starting with the interface, I need to handle 16-bit inputs for nine data channels and a 4-bit select signal. The key insight is that the select range only covers 0-8, with the remaining 8 select values (9-15) requiring all output bits to be set to '1'. This means I can't use a simple case statement without handling the unused cases explicitly.

For the implementation, I'll use a case statement that covers all possible select values. For select values 0-8, I'll directly assign the corresponding input channel. For select values 9-15, I'll assign all output bits to '1' using a constant value. This approach ensures clean and readable code while meeting the specification.

